:rsm:
# Understanding Merge Sort

:abstract:

  Merge sort is an elegant divide-and-conquer algorithm that achieves optimal $O(n \log n)$ time complexity. This document explains its mechanics through interactive visualization and formal analysis.

::

## The Algorithm

:definition:
:label: merge-sort-def

:span: {:label: merge-sort-term} Merge sort :: is a comparison-based sorting algorithm that divides the input array into halves, recursively sorts each half, and then merges the sorted halves back together.

::

The elegance of :ref:merge-sort-term:: lies in its simplicity\: sorting two halves is easier than sorting the whole, and merging two sorted arrays is straightforward.

```
:lang: python
def merge_sort(arr):
    if len(arr) <= 1:
        return arr

    mid = len(arr) // 2
    left = merge_sort(arr[:mid])
    right = merge_sort(arr[mid:])

    return merge(left, right)
```

